// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 04-expressions/primitive_str_member_read_capability_neg_66.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A dot member read on a primitive str parameter is syntax the parser and
// binder accept, but str is not a nominal scalar with lowered fields. The
// string-length fold only applies to string-literal-initialized locals, so a
// str parameter stays unsupported. The checker body slice drains the free
// function body with the unsupported-construct code ZOM4099 instead of
// reaching a missing-fact invariant.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/04-expressions/primitive_str_member_read_capability_neg_66.zom:2:12
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |
// CHECK-LITERAL: 2 |     return s.length;
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |            ^~~~~~~~
// CHECK-LITERAL: 1 error generated.
